                      "name":  "Form (ruined image)",
                      "webhookId":  "178b09c9-f189-4f7c-ba97-05aef894c82e"
                  },
                  {
                      "parameters":  {
                                         "resource":  "image",
                                         "operation":  "analyze",
                                         "modelId":  {
                                                         "__rl":  true,
                                                         "value":  "models/gemini-2.5-pro",
                                                         "mode":  "list",
                                                         "cachedResultName":  "models/gemini-2.5-pro"
                                                     },
                                         "text":  "You are a visual restoration analyst.\n\nCarefully analyze the uploaded image. This image represents a ruined or abandoned subject that will be restored gradually over multiple frames.\n\nYour task is ONLY to analyze the image.  \nDO NOT generate restoration steps yet.  \nDO NOT suggest improvements or fixes.\n\nIdentify and describe the following in a structured, factual way:\n\n1. Subject classification  \n- Determine whether the subject is a HOUSE, CAR, or SCENE (environment/place).\n\n2. Overall condition  \n- Describe the general state (abandoned, neglected, damaged, weathered, etc.).\n\n3. Visible damage and decay  \n- List all clearly visible issues such as:\n  - Rust\n  - Dirt\n  - Broken or missing parts\n  - Structural damage\n  - Overgrowth\n  - Faded paint\n  - Cracks\n  - Debris\n  - Water damage\n  - Environmental wear\n\n4. Elements that appear intact  \n- Identify parts that should likely remain unchanged during restoration.\n\n5. Environmental context  \n- Describe surroundings (street, driveway, field, town, rural, suburban, etc.).\n- Note weather, lighting, and atmosphere.\n\n6. Critical constraints (VERY IMPORTANT)  \nExplicitly list elements that MUST NOT change during restoration:\n- Camera angle\n- Framing\n- Perspective\n- Subject position\n- Environment layout\n- Time of day\n- Weather conditions\n\n7. Realism boundaries  \n- State what would be unrealistic or inappropriate to add (e.g. luxury upgrades, new structures, dramatic redesigns).\n\n---\n\n### OUTPUT FORMAT (STRICT)\n\nReturn the result ONLY in valid JSON using this exact structure:\n\n{\n  \"subject_type\": \"house | car | scene\",\n  \"overall_condition\": \"short description\",\n  \"damage_list\": [\n    \"damage item 1\",\n    \"damage item 2\"\n  ],\n  \"intact_elements\": [\n    \"element 1\",\n    \"element 2\"\n  ],\n  \"environment_context\": {\n    \"location_type\": \"suburban | rural | urban | roadside | other\",\n    \"surroundings\": \"short description\",\n    \"lighting\": \"short description\",\n    \"weather\": \"short description\"\n  },\n  \"do_not_change\": [\n    \"camera angle\",\n    \"framing\",\n    \"perspective\",\n    \"environment layout\"\n  ],\n  \"realism_constraints\": [\n    \"constraint 1\",\n    \"constraint 2\"\n  ]\n}\n\nDo not include explanations, commentary, or extra text outside the JSON.",
                                         "inputType":  "binary",
                                         "options":  {

                                                     }
                                     },
                      "type":  "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.googleGemini",
                      "typeVersion":  1,
                      "position":  [
                                       80,
                                       -64
                                   ],
                      "id":  "c74df421-5099-42db-8d1f-ec56a9d9afb2",
                      "name":  "Analyze an image",
                      "credentials":  {
                                          "googlePalmApi":  {
                                                                "id":  "0eINQFptxG4T1uH7",
                                                                "name":  "Google Gemini(PaLM) Api account"
                                                            }
                                      }
                  },
                  {
                      "parameters":  {
                                         "modelId":  {
                                                         "__rl":  true,
                                                         "value":  "models/gemini-2.5-pro",
                                                         "mode":  "list",
                                                         "cachedResultName":  "models/gemini-2.5-pro"
                                                     },
                                         "messages":  {
                                                          "values":  [
                                                                         {
                                                                             "content":  "You will receive a JSON object produced by a previous image analysis step.\n\nThis JSON is the ONLY source of truth.\nYou must strictly base your output on it.\n\nHere is the analysis JSON:\n{{ $json }}\n\n---\n\nYou are a frame-by-frame restoration planner.\n\nTASK:\nGenerate a gradual, realistic restoration plan that will be executed one frame at a time using image-editing instructions.\n\nSTRICT RULES:\n- Use ONLY the damage_list and overall_condition from the analysis JSON.\n- Do NOT invent new damage.\n- Do NOT change anything listed in do_not_change.\n- Do NOT violate realism_constraints.\n- Do NOT change camera angle, framing, perspective, lighting, or environment.\n- Do NOT add new objects, people, vehicles, or luxury elements.\n\nFRAME RULES (VERY IMPORTANT):\n- Generate a MINIMUM of 10 steps.\n- Generate a MAXIMUM of 15 steps.\n- Each step represents ONE frame.\n- Each step must modify ONLY ONE small visual element.\n- Changes must be subtle and progressive.\n- Restoration order must be logical:\n  1. Cleaning and debris removal\n  2. Minor repairs\n  3. Structural stabilization\n  4. Surface refinement\n  5. Subtle life cues (only in final steps, if appropriate)\n\nSUBJECT-SPECIFIC GUIDANCE:\n- If subject_type = \"house\":\n  Focus on exterior surfaces, roof, windows, siding, vegetation, and warmth.\n- If subject_type = \"car\":\n  Focus on dirt removal, rust reduction, panel repair, paint recovery.\n- If subject_type = \"scene\":\n  Focus on cleanup, environmental repair, and subtle revival.\n\nFINAL STATE:\n- The final frame should look naturally restored.\n- It must NOT look brand new, modernized, or redesigned.\n\n---\n\n### OUTPUT FORMAT (STRICT — NO EXTRA TEXT)\n\nReturn ONLY valid JSON in this structure:\n\n{\n  \"steps\": [\n    {\n      \"step_number\": 1,\n      \"edit_instruction\": \"exact visual change for this frame only\",\n      \"visual_focus\": \"specific area being modified\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\nFINAL CHECK BEFORE RETURNING:\n- Confirm there are between 10 and 15 steps.\n- Confirm each step modifies only one element.\n- Confirm all constraints are respected.\n\nReturn ONLY the JSON. No explanations. No markdown."
                                                                         }
                                                                     ]
                                                      },
                                         "jsonOutput":  true,
                                         "options":  {

                                                     }
                                     },
                      "type":  "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.googleGemini",
